# Implementation Plan - Fix Telegram Bot Message Delivery

Fix the issue where the bot fails to initialize due to a variable name mismatch in the [.env](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/.env) file and improve the robustness of callback query handling.

## Proposed Changes

### Configuration and Initialization

#### [MODIFY] [bot.py](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/bot.py)

- Update the token loading logic to check for both `BOT_TOKEN` and `TOKEN` to ensure compatibility with the current [.env](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/.env) file.
- Add a try-except block around the `bot.answer_callback_query` call in the PDF sending section of the [callback_query](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/bot.py#355-412) handler. This will prevent "query is too old" errors from causing the entire handler to fail and log an error.

```python
# Change in 19
BOT_TOKEN = os.getenv("BOT_TOKEN") or os.getenv("TOKEN")

# Change in 391
try:
    bot.answer_callback_query(call.id, "📄 Enviando PDF...")
except Exception as e:
    logging.warning(f"Error respondiendo callback PDF: {e}")
```

